/* The icon Windows shows on DreamQuest.exe itself, in Explorer, on a shortcut
   and in Alt-Tab. The window's own icon is set at runtime from art/app_icon.png;
   this one has to be compiled in, because Explorer never runs the program.

   Built by build.ps1 with windres, from art/dreamquest.ico -- both that and the
   .png come out of tools/make_titleart.ps1. Lowest id wins in Explorer, so the
   application icon is 1. */
1 ICON "art/dreamquest.ico"

/* And the manifest (resource type 24, id 1 for an exe), for both exes. It
   replaces the default one MinGW links in, so it repeats that one's two parts
   (run as the user who started it; the Windows versions it is written for)
   and adds a third: UTF-8 as the program's code page. Saves live under the
   user's profile (UserFiles in save.cpp), and a profile folder can have any
   letter in its name; without this a narrow path with an accent in it fails
   to open. The manifest itself carries no comment: Windows refuses to start
   a program whose manifest is not strict XML, and an XML comment may not
   contain two hyphens in a row -- a comment there once stopped the exe. */
1 24 "tools/app.manifest"
